-  hundreds of paths); the `zeroclaw` CLI help text, `~/.zeroclaw` config dir,
-  `ZEROCLAW_*` env vars, systemd unit and web dashboard strings are upstream's.
-- An already-configured vendor provider with its own `api_key` still works; only
-  the subscription-login families are refused at the factory.
-- Codex (`requires_openai_auth`) and Claude setup-token credentials already on
-  disk are not refused at request time, only at Quickstart.
+  hundreds of paths); `~/.zeroclaw`, `ZEROCLAW_*` env vars, the systemd unit,
+  the web dashboard and non-English locale strings are upstream's. The companion
+  desktop app, firmware and OpenClaw migration keep their real artifact names.
+- An operator-configured vendor provider with its own `api_key` still works; it
+  is not the default and holds a key outside OpenVault.
 - Whether OpenVault needs a seat token on `/v1` or serves `/v1/models`, and
   whether it registers tool ids under kind `runtime` and channel ids under
   `service`, is not measured. The gate sends no seat token.
 - Conversation text can still persist outside the session store: memory
   backends, the ACP session store, cost and observability logs. Not gated.
-- Cron delivery to a channel (`build_channel_map`) and one-shot sends are not
-  behind the leave-machine ask; only channel startup is.
+- Launch dependency: with no OpenVault answering at `NETIE_OPENVAULT_URL`, every
